  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Peace, Justice and Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program consists of two core components: (1) gender justice and legal empowerment, and (2) interfaith dialogue and youth resilience. The first component builds the capacity of young lawyers and media graduates to advocate for gender equality and human rights, while increasing rural women&#x2019;s legal awareness on divorce, custody, and protection from violence. It also strengthens public debate on women&#x2019;s rights through media outreach, legal initiatives, and policy advocacy. The second component fosters understanding and cooperation between Christian and Muslim students, faculty, and religious leaders through dialogue, joint activities, and cultural&#x2011;heritage learning. It broadens public engagement with interfaith principles through multimedia storytelling and digital outreach, while also enhancing young people&#x2019;s psychosocial resilience and leadership skills through training and community service.</narrative>
  </description>
